Please take a closer look.

262
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:36,977
Surely you know Hierophant
isn't that careless.

263
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:41,178
He wouldn't just stay on the enemy's
back without a plan in the wings.

264
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:49,540
He's not chopped in half!

265
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:54,180
He's turned into a snake-like thing,
and he's slithering into my ear!

266
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:08,800
Oh, my arm is moving on its own!

267
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:12,500
No, it's coming in!

268
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:22,861
I told you before, my stand was in your
blind spot, and your scythe couldn't cut it.

269
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:26,977
Now then, unless you'd like to
be destroyed from the inside out,

270
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:30,097
how about you do me a favor
and heal the cuts on my arm?

271
00:17:30,180 --> 00:17:32,560
Anything is possible in a dream, right?

272
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,960
So healing a cut should be easy.

273
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:36,850
Right!

274
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:49,296
All right, everyone.

275
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,461
Time to wake up.

276
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:56,040
Come on, Polnareff. Up and at him.

277
00:17:56,220 --> 00:17:58,632
There's a nice breakfast waiting for you.

278
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:05,126
I feel like I had a
terrible dream last night.

279
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:06,221
You and me both.

280
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:11,048
I can't remember it, but I have the
sneaking suspicion that it was terrifying.

281
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:15,150
Kakuine!

282
00:18:15,233 --> 00:18:16,063
Are you okay?

283
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:18,437
How are you like a deranged
lunatic last night?

284
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:20,638
You even carved letters in your arm.

285
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:23,997
Wait, what?

286
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:25,660
Where did the wound go?

287
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:29,540
Alright, I think I'll change
the baby's diaper now.

288
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:32,160
What in the world?

289
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:35,260
It's morning, Sleepyhead.

290
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:38,457
He seems to be getting along
famously with the baby.

291
00:18:38,540 --> 00:18:40,716
Maybe I just dreamed the whole thing.

292
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:43,680
Well then, did you have a good rest?

293
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:45,860
Oh, well, never mind.

294
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:54,655
Everyone's forgotten.

295
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:58,260
A stand whose very existence
is completely forgotten.

296
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:00,820
What a strange creature.

297
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:03,940
But I haven't forgotten anything.

298
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:08,595
Since I brought my stand into the
dream with me, my memories are intact.

299
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:10,630
Injury you.

300
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:13,140
We'll take you to a nearby town.

301
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:15,754
You need to be returned to your mother.

302
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,980
However, don't come
anywhere near us again.

303
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:21,575
If you do, you'll have to be punished.

304
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:26,260
In a manner such as this.

305
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:29,540
Is that my poop?

306
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:37,680
Oh, Cockyooey.

307
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,059
I see you've made some baby
food for the little lad.

308
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:43,000
Yes, good work.

309
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:45,378
I'm sure he must be starving by now.

310
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:49,560
Hey, no, you wouldn't!

311
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,420
Eat up!

312
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:55,446
These yum-yums are delicious!

313
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:57,320
Say-ya!

314
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:02,520
This again?

315
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:03,958
What's the problem?

316
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:06,335
It's as if he doesn't like this stuff.

317
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,951
At this rate, I'll have to force-feed him.

318
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:10,010
Stop!

319
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:13,140
You can't force it, Mr. Joestar.

320
00:20:13,460 --> 00:20:16,317
If you do, he'll just end
up hating it even more.

321
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:18,620
In special cases like this.

322
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:21,480
A goji-goo?

323
00:20:21,660 --> 00:20:24,060
A goji-goo-ji-goo-ji-goo?

324
00:20:24,540 --> 00:20:26,580
A goji-goo-ji-goo-ji-goo?

325
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:36,940
I told you it was
delicious, but I'm bummed.

326
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:48,517
Joestar and the others have now
crossed the Arabian Peninsula

327
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:51,277
and are currently making
their way across the Red Sea?

328
00:20:51,360 --> 00:20:54,600
as they prepare to enter Egypt, but...

329
00:20:57,140 --> 00:20:58,937
Hey, old man. Something's off.

330
00:20:59,020 --> 00:21:00,961
You're going the wrong direction.

331
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:05,800
If you're headed to Egypt, shouldn't
you be traveling directly west? Hmm?

332
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:09,431
You seem to be heading toward that island.

333
00:21:10,180 --> 00:21:11,980
That's right. Nice deduction.

334
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:15,037
I've had my reasons for
keeping this to myself.

335
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:18,757
But before we arrive in Egypt,
we need to make a slight detour.

336
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:21,193
Someone is waiting for us on the island.

337
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:22,350
Hmm.

338
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:23,590
Hmm.

339
00:21:23,673 --> 00:21:25,958
He's a man who is extremely
important to our journey.

340
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:28,820
What is that supposed to mean?

341
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:53,417
And dance, don't you know?

342
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:54,977
If you move too quick!

343
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:58,097
They're falling down like a domino.

344
00:21:58,180 --> 00:22:00,757
All the birds are men by the Nile.

345
00:22:00,840 --> 00:22:04,397
They've got the money on
a bed Called crocodiles.

346
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:07,377
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

347
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:09,737
Foreign types with a hookah. I say!

348
00:22:09,820 --> 00:22:10,717
Walk

349
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:17,757
like

350
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:18,670
an Egyptian.

351
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:32,137
The blonde waitresses take their trays.

352
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:34,137
Spin around and they cross the floor.

353
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:35,657
They've got the moves.

354
00:22:35,740 --> 00:22:38,637
You drop your drink, tick off books.

355
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:40,697
They're like the punk and the metal band.

356
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:42,260
When the buzzer rings?

357
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:44,937
They're walking like an Egyptian.

358
00:22:45,020 --> 00:22:47,680
All the kids in the marketplace say?

359
00:22:59,980 --> 00:23:02,000
I ended up killing my friend.

360
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:04,498
There's nothing I could possibly do.

361
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:07,581
Allow me to thank you for
freeing me from the lab.

362
00:23:07,740 --> 00:23:09,817
I wouldn't believe it
if it wasn't right here.

363
00:23:09,900 --> 00:23:11,429
Tell me your three wishes.

364
00:23:11,540 --> 00:23:14,100
Do you have the ability to revive someone?
